description:
Write the save system a finished game needs: a readable, versioned save file with a checksum, migration from the previous version, a fallback to the backup when the main save is damaged, and the high-score table.

```cpp
struct Score { int points; std::string name; };
struct SaveData
{
    int level{ 1 };
    int coins{ 0 };
    std::vector<std::string> unlocked;     // area names, in the order they were unlocked
    std::vector<Score> scores;             // best first, at most 5
};
enum class LoadResult { Ok, Missing, Damaged, TooNew };

std::uint32_t fnv1a(const std::string& text);
std::string writeSave(const SaveData& s);
LoadResult loadSave(const std::string& text, SaveData& out);
int chooseSave(const std::string& primary, const std::string& backup, SaveData& out);
int addScore(std::vector<Score>& table, const std::string& name, int points);
```

**fnv1a** is the 32-bit FNV-1a hash: start at `2166136261`; for each byte, XOR it in, then multiply by `16777619` (arithmetic wraps around at 2³²).

**The file** (version 2), lines ending in `\n`:

```
xenon-save 2
level 3
coins 120
unlocked forest,caves
score 1200 Sam
score 900 Alex Smith
checksum 1a2b3c4d
```

`unlocked` lists the areas separated by commas (the line is written even when empty: `unlocked `, with nothing after the space). Each `score` line is the points then the name (which may contain spaces). The last line is `checksum` followed by the FNV-1a hash of **everything before it** (all the earlier lines with their `\n`), as 8 lower-case hex digits.

**loadSave**:
- An empty text is `Missing`.
- The first line must be `xenon-save N`. N greater than 2 is `TooNew`; N must be 1 or 2.
- The checksum line must be last and must match; otherwise, or for any line that cannot be read, the result is `Damaged`. Lines may end with `\r\n` (the checksum is computed over the text as stored, so a file with `\r\n` endings hashes them too).
- **Version 1** files had `gold` instead of `coins` and no `unlocked` line: load them into the version 2 data.
- Unknown lines are ignored, so later versions can add lines. `level` must be at least 1 and `coins` at least 0, or it is `Damaged`.
- Only on `Ok` is `out` changed.

**chooseSave** loads the primary text into `out` and returns 1; if that is not `Ok`, it tries the backup and returns 2; if neither loads, `out` becomes a default `SaveData` and it returns 0.

**addScore** inserts a score into the table, best first, **after** existing equal scores, keeps at most 5, and returns the new score's rank (1 to 5), or 0 if it did not make the table.

